WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:02.902
-Our first guest tonight is
a legendary comedian and actor

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.303
who you know from films such as

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:07.106
"Uncut Gems," "The Wedding
Singer," and "Happy Gilmore,"

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.008
and, of course, his time on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.944
He executive produced
and stars in "Hustle,"

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.380
which is in select theaters now
and on Netflix tomorrow.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.782
Please welcome back to the show
our very good friend,

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:18.751
Adam Sandler, everybody!

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:22.755
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:29.495 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:36.235 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:39.239
Welcome back!
-Thank you. Hi, everybody.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.940
Thank you.
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.776
-I'm so -- that was --

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.511
That Post Malone thing
was so fun.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.013
-We got after it.
We got after it a little bit.

00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:49.616
-How did nobody throw up?

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.950
-Um...

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.352
I'm not saying nobody did.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.586
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.055
The magic of editing
is very helpful.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.224
-Oh, my God
-Adam, a little worried.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.725
You got a --
Something happened here.

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:00.593
You got a black eye.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.228
-I wish it was...

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.297
I've been telling people that
I fought Jake Paul.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.032
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.802
I was just in bed and my phone
flew up and --

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:13.740
So I just -- I've been
talking about it today.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.241
I feel like an idiot
saying it again,

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.843
but I was stuffed in a bed.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:21.648
You know when they tuck you in
the bed and they don't un--

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.416
they tuck it under the thing?
-Yeah.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.750
-Like that?

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.153
You make the decision before
you get in bed, you go,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.521
"Do I want to struggle
pulling that?

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.123
Let me just get in there."

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.057
I didn't pull,
so I got in there,

00:01:32.057 --> 00:01:33.325
and then, like, 4:00
in the morning I was like,

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:34.794
"Why did I...?"

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:38.597
My stupid phone was --
I was kicking the thing,

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.767
and it flew in the air
and hit me in the face.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.202
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:45.071
-Don't let anybody tell you
that's an embarrassing story.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.107
That's a great way
to get a black eye.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:51.177
Fortunately, I guess that
happened after this.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.611
At least you did not have a --
-Yes.

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:55.447
-You gave the commencement
at your alma mater.

00:01:55.447 --> 00:01:57.349
-Yes, NYU. Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:58.518
Great day.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.552
[ Applause ]

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.720
-This is stressful, though,
right?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.988
-Oh, my God!

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.156
Once I said that I'm doing that,

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:06.359
I was so terrified
to do the speech,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.559
because it meant a lot to me.

00:02:07.559 --> 00:02:08.828
I wanted everybody
to be happy.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.496
I knew everyone's
families were there.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.364
It's...anyways.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:14.200
I worked hard
and we had a great time.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.501
Do you know --
I'll tell you this.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.169
This is funny.

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.739
Fred, I think you'll like this.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.474
When I was, like, getting...

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:25.411
I did "Punch Drunk Love,"
and I was so excited

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.648
I did a cool movie,
blah blah blah blah.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:32.752
I was like, I bet my NYU, those
guys will like that movie there.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.888
'Cause I was always doing
comedies and stuff.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.756
It's pretty serious
at that school.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.724
So I was like, "They'll like
'Punch Drunk Love.'"

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.659
So me and Paul Thomas Anderson

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.895
got invited to talk to
the film school,

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.831
and I remember walking
out there going,

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:48.167
"This is pretty cool, man.
I made something of myself."

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:52.037
I sit down and I'm with PTA,
next to him,

00:02:52.037 --> 00:02:54.340
and literally every question --

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.875
"Any questions for these guys?"

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.144
Every question, "Mr. Anderson,

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:01.347
uh, what camera did
you use in 'Boogie Nights'?"

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.416
Literally, like, 30 in a row.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.851
I was going...

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:05.985
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.054
They're just asking
Mr. Anderson everything,

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.955
because he's the king of film.

00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:11.291
And I was just like,

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.192
"You know, when I did
Bobby Boucher..."

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:14.793
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:15.861
Anyways.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.030
-You got that,

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.032
where you get sweaty and
you start looking for it.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.801
-I'm like, do I look at Paul,
too, and ask him something?

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.671
How did you do --

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:25.771
-It's fantastic.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.907
We've talked in the past
about your girls,

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.876
16 and 13?
-Yes.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.878
-They're growing up.
-Yeah. It hurts.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.246
It hurts.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:36.683
So that my daughters
and that boys are now

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.719
going be involved
with their life and that.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.753
-How are you feeling
about that?

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.554
-Very nervous very and tense.

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:44.190
I'm not very comfortable
with that.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.525
I think I'm more comfortable

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:48.061
with my wife
bringing home somebody.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.195
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:52.131
I would actually feel
like, alright.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.999
I have more in common with,
like --

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:56.569
boy that is age, 13 to 16,

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.338
I literally have nothing
to talk to them about.

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.905
My wife, if she brought home,
I'd be like,

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:04.277
"Hey, man.
You go to my golf club, right?

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.544
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:07.646
Have fun with my wife.

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:10.783
Just don't stay out too late."

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.384
16, driving?

00:04:12.384 --> 00:04:13.819
-Yes.
-I mean, L.A. kid.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:14.887
Got to learn how to drive,
right?

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.322
-It comes out of nowhere.
You're gonna see.

00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:19.391
All of the sudden,
your nice, little kids are like,

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:20.626
their friends are are
all driving.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:25.765
My daughter is getting her
license next month.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.733
She drives around with
the Driver's Ed guy,

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:30.602
which is cool, but then
she's got to practice with us,

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:31.837
me and my wife.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.806
And you're in the...

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.441
The Driver's Ed guy
has the brake.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.010
So he's, like, safe.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.380
I'm with my 16-year-old
daughter, and I don't --

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.681
I'm nervous for her.

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.617
'Cause, like, there's
a partition and you can't...

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.118
I don't know how
I'm gonna hit the brake.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.387
Like, dive over and push on it.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.722
So I'm just like...

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.124
I don't want her to get hurt.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.593
Me, I don't think
I'm going to die.

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:57.463
Which I'm almost to like,
"You know what?

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:58.765
I've had enough."

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.065
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.167
I don't mind me dying,
but this kid's got a nice --

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.503
So I want to help her.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.371
So when she went to
school one day,

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:09.876
I went out in our family car
and sneakily installed a brake.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.178
I had one of the guys that
knows what he is doing

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.412
put a brake on my side,

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:14.714
so just in case, when
we're driving around...

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.448
-You have a driver's
side brake on your car now?

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:18.250
-Just, like, a pull thing.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.219
Nobody knows about it.
My kid don't know about it.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.220
I never had to use it with her.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.289
My wife, though,
we were driving,

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.224
we got into the car,

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.393
and she was like,
"Before we go to dinner,

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.895
I'd love to go to
this antique store,"

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.564
and I was just like --

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.865
chhhhkkkkk.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:36.702
I don't know.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.971
I feel -- that's a little,
whatever.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.606
A little wacky.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.109
-You got -- we've talked
about the first bat mitzvah.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.543
You've got another one coming
up? Or have you had it?

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:47.913
-We had the bat mitzvah
a couple weeks ago.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:49.748
It was the Sweet 16.

00:05:49.748 --> 00:05:50.883
-Got them both out of
the way now?

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.518
-Cost a lot of money,
those things.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.421
-While you were watching theirs,

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.789
did it remind you of
your bar mitzvah?

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:57.957
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:01.794
My kid's bat mitzvah was like,
an extravaganza.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.129
I don't even know
what's the hell's happening.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:06.765
All insane dancing and
everyone's --

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:10.435
there's sexuality
running around.

00:06:10.435 --> 00:06:11.838
But my bar mitzvah was

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:14.273
just in the basement
at my parent's house.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:17.476
I think we went to
the temple in the day.

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:20.913
My parents maybe bought some
meatballs or something,

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.015
put it downstairs
in the basement.

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.417
Some neighbors came over,
I think.

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:27.686
But that was the first time
I jammed.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:31.457
My guitar teacher had a band,
and he was the band.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:32.592
He let me play "My Sharona."

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.827
I played "My Sharona"
when I was 13,

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:37.129
and all my friends
gathered around

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:39.765
and I played "My Sharona"
and I was singing.

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:41.000
All my New Hampshire friends
were like,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.268
"Sandler can sing, man."

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:46.305
I was looking people directly
in the eyes, just going --

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:47.640
[ Imitates guitar ]

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.075
That was, like,
my first time --

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.309
-That's very formative.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.211
I feel like that's what you
would want to hear

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.279
about a bar mitzvah.

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:54.780
Like, you crossed a threshold
there.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.515
-I swear to God, I think I went
to bed that night going,

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:59.652
"I gotta...I'm gonna be
a rock star one day.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:02.154
And then, I swear to God,
I went to NYU

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:05.390
and I thought I was gonna be
a rock star until I got to NYU,

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.994
and in my hallway, there were,
like, five other guys

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:12.197
playing guitar,
just doing everything.

00:07:12.197 --> 00:07:14.233
[ Imitates guitar ] Everything.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:17.236
I was just going,
"I gotta be a comedian.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:19.638
There's no way I'm gonna
compete with that."

00:07:19.638 --> 00:07:22.107
-I want to talk about
the new film, which is great.

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:25.545
We'll be right back with
more from Adam Sandler.

